Weeping Sītā sets straw barrier and turns Rāvaṇa toward own wives --- Sītā warns coveting others wives ruins kings and dooms jeweled Laṅkā --- Sītā vows sunlight-like oneness with Rāma and demands reunion --- Sītā warns enraged Rāma spares none and his arrows approach --- Sītā scorns theft from empty hermitage as dog before tigers --- Sītā warns no Kubēra mountain or Varuṇa hall escapes Dāśarathi shafts
